      "created_at": "2011-11-07T03:04:49.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>During a game over the weekend, a conversation with Christopher and some other folks came up around the flavor text on Living Conflagration. I have a variety of Egyptian-style fonts (as a role-playing game GM, they’ve come in handy in the past), and I thought the font looked familiar, but I haven’t made the time to translate it.</p>\n<p>So I decided I needed to resolve that issue. <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=9\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\"></p>\n<p>After a little time comparing fonts, I determined the font was Hieroglify (or at least something close to it). It only took me “_ _ rist _ _ er   _ _ _   _ _ _ _” before I knew what it said, but I finished the exercise, anyway.  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=9\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\"></p>\n<p>Has anyone else worked through this?  8)</p>\n<p>Rabit</p>",
